WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.040
In the year 2039,
new developments in virtual reality

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.920
could give 'connecting with someone
you fancy' a whole new meaning.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.120
Facebook already hosts a show
called Virtually Dating,

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.720
where couples strap on headsets

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.640
and virtually spend time
in exotic locations.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.200
Imagine if you could go on a date

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.440
without the commitment of having
to actually be there in person.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.080
A 21st Century romance?

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.400
Or just another way to
bash into the furniture

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.640
of your ridiculously
small housing pod

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.480
before you take off your headset
only to remember

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.040
there's no one there.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.880
Alternatively, maybe your
VR date will go so well

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:41.120
you'll question why you need a real
life partner in the first place.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.560
A company in Japan
is already offering men

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.600
the chance to marry
their favourite anime characters.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.760
Will you be professing
your lifelong commitment

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.680
to a 3D hologram in a virtual chapel?

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.600
If you're a woman,
the answer may well be no.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.440
Even though research shows
that people are more likely

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.640
to open up to a machine
than a person.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.120
It also shows that women

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.120
are less likely to try
virtual reality than men.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:09.120
A company's recent solution?
Turn the headsets pink.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.040
It didn't solve the problem.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.160
If by 2039 VR is more widespread,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.760
could connecting to your partner,
emotionally or physically,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.040
simply mean digging out
your VR toolkit

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:27.000
and plugging one of a number of,
ahem, devices into a USB port

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.040
or does the very thought of this
make you want to split up?

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:31.440
Or throw up?

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.560
If looking the one you love
in the eye is more your thing,

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.040
you might prefer glasses
that use face-analysing algorithms

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.280
to scientifically reveal
when someone finds you attractive.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.040
A way to make dating
less time-consuming

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.800
or a virtual slap in the face
when you discover

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.040
that everyone you're pretty much
definitely sure fancies you, doesn't.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.960
Digital technology is often
criticised for increasing loneliness

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.000
as people turn more to their screens
for support, rather than each other.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.480
However, by 2039
we could be using dating apps

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.200
to connect with a multitude of people

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.520
in a variety of new,
non-romantic ways.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.480
Will finding a partner
to settle down with

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.360
be something your parents used to do?

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:18.320
Either way, with nightclubs
across the UK closing down

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.480
and fewer young people
drinking alcohol,

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.320
it seems like the days of...

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.280
and having one too many of...

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.080
only to wake up with...

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.440
are probably numbered.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.480
So if we're still going
on real dates with real people,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.600
we'll probably need new venues.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.480
For example, a trampoline park.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.200
According to a recent report

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.240
there's been an overwhelming
rise in trampolining.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.680
Imagine if this was where
you're meeting a hot

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.360
and very sweaty date in 2039.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.520
New kinds of
immersive cinema experiences,

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.840
such as 4D or 5D,

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.800
might also pave the way
for virtual reality films,

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.240
which would make the cinema
the perfect place for a date in 2039

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.000
with friends, partners
or anyone in between,

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.120
just  like it's always been.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:15.380
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

